    "end": "The compromise: lukewarm drizzle.",
    "caption": "The dial is just inside that front door.\n\nLuke: 390,000 people, a 24-hour day, no moons, and one thermostat, in the hallway of a rented flat. Priya likes it tropical. Ellie likes it snowing. Neither has read the tenancy agreement, which is very clear that the weather is shared. The neighbours keep a parasol and a shovel by the door and no longer ask.\n\nI was there for one morning. I got sunburnt and snowed on before lunch.\n\n(On Earth, a 2015 study in Nature Climate Change found that the standard formula for office temperatures was worked out for the metabolism of a forty-year-old man. On Luke, it's worked out by whoever touched the dial last.)\n\nWho in your house is in charge of the dial?"
  },
  "first_comment": "Week two of drizzle. Priya has bought a very small heater.",
